---
title: "Organizations"
description: "Select an organization and manage its members, invitations, OAuth clients, and payment method."
---

An organization owns projects, members, OAuth clients, the payment method, and
10DLC registrations. Membership belongs to the organization: a member has one
organization role, and an invitation grants access to all of the
organization's projects.

```sh
photon org list
photon org show
photon org use pho_org_01k9yq3m7d2c8x4v6b5n0p1r2s
```

## Command overview

```text
photon org
├── list
├── show
├── use <organization-id>
├── clear
├── leave [--yes] [--idempotency-key <key>]
├── member
│   ├── list
│   ├── invite --email <email> --role <member|viewer> [--idempotency-key <key>]
│   ├── edit <account-id> --role <admin|member|viewer> [--idempotency-key <key>]
│   └── remove <account-id> [--yes] [--idempotency-key <key>]
├── invitation
│   ├── list
│   ├── preview [--token-file <path>]
│   ├── accept [--token-file <path>] [--idempotency-key <key>]
│   └── revoke <invitation-id> [--yes] [--idempotency-key <key>]
├── oauth-client ...         # see OAuth clients
└── billing
    └── payment-method ...   # see Payment method
```

